landing.reference.hero.text.1=.NET web framework
landing.reference.hero.text.2=A lightweight, modern web framework for structured UI, REST integration and clean architecture.
landing.reference.hero.text.3=WebExpress is a comprehensive all-in-one framework for .NET 10 and Kestrel that embodies an Edge to Cloud strategy. Through its modular plugin system, it integrates web applications, reusable UI controls, and REST APIs into a unified host. By providing all fundamental functions in a single package, WebExpress eliminates complexity and ensures a scalable solution that adapts effortlessly to diverse infrastructure demands.
landing.reference.hero.link.1=Get Started
landing.reference.hero.link.2=View on GitHub
landing.reference.hero.highlight.1=⚙ Lightweight & efficient
landing.reference.hero.highlight.2=🧩 Plugin-first architecture
landing.reference.hero.highlight.3=🔐 HTTPS & HTTP/2 ready
landing.reference.introduction.text.1=Introduction
landing.reference.introduction.text.2=Getting Started with WebExpress
landing.reference.introduction.text.3=WebExpress provides a .NET 10 host for modular web applications. WebCore manages plugins, applications, routing and HTTP endpoints on Kestrel. WebUI supplies reusable controls, WebApp adds application templates and REST integration, and WebIndex provides full-text indexing and search.
landing.reference.introduction.text.4=Installation
landing.reference.introduction.text.5=For development, install the .NET 10 SDK and build the host or a tutorial application. For deployment, download a WebExpress release for your target platform and follow its runtime requirements. The installation guide covers Raspberry Pi setup, systemd integration and production HTTPS.
landing.reference.introduction.list.1=- [Installation guide](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress/blob/main/docs/installation_guide.md)\n- [Latest releases](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress/releases)
landing.reference.introduction.text.6=First Steps
landing.reference.introduction.text.7=To create an application, start with the HelloWorld tutorial and its separate plugin and host projects. Configure the host in `settings/webexpress.settings.json`, place packaged plugins in the configured `PackagePath` and start WebExpress from its installation directory.
landing.reference.introduction.list.2=- [HelloWorld tutorial](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress.Tutorial.HelloWorld#readme)\n- [WebUI tutorial](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress.Tutorial.WebUI#readme)\n- [WebApp tutorial](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress.Tutorial.WebApp#readme)\n- [WebIndex tutorial](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress.Tutorial.WebIndex#readme)
landing.reference.introduction.text.8=Core Concepts
landing.reference.introduction.text.9=The framework separates hosting from application features. Plugins define applications and endpoints, while UI controls and fragments compose their user interfaces. Choose the libraries that your application requires.
landing.reference.introduction.list.3=- [WebExpress.WebCore: runtime](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress.WebCore#readme)\n- [WebExpress.WebUI: controls](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress.WebUI#readme)\n- [WebExpress.WebApp: application templates](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress.WebApp#readme)\n- [WebExpress.WebIndex: search index](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress.WebIndex#readme)
landing.reference.introduction.text.10=Minimal configuration (`settings/webexpress.settings.json`)
landing.reference.introduction.text.11=For local development, save this file in the settings directory under the host's working directory and start WebExpress from that working directory. The example listens at http://localhost:8080/. Endpoints defines the listener, while ExternalUri sets the base address used for generated URLs. The package, asset and data paths are relative to the working directory.
landing.reference.introduction.text.12=For configuration overrides, WebExpress merges the other JSON files in the settings directory in alphabetical order, then the main settings file, followed by environment variables prefixed with `WEBEXPRESS_`. Plugin settings belong under `Plugins` in a section named after the plugin ID. Restart the host after changing its settings.
landing.reference.introduction.text.13=For production HTTPS, configure an HTTPS endpoint and its certificate reference. The [configuration guide](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress/blob/main/docs/config.md) explains certificate settings, environment overrides and additional server options.
landing.reference.introduction.text.14=For the full API documentation see the [WebCore API docs](https://webexpress-framework.github.io/WebExpress.WebCore/) and the [WebUI API docs](https://webexpress-framework.github.io/WebExpress.WebUI/).
landing.reference.contribute.text.1=Community
landing.reference.contribute.text.2=Contribute to WebExpress
landing.reference.contribute.text.3=WebExpress is open source under the MIT license. Contributions include bug reports, feature ideas, documentation and translations. Please open an issue before starting larger changes to agree on the scope.
landing.reference.contribute.text.4=Ways to contribute
landing.reference.contribute.list.1=- Report bugs through the GitHub issue tracker.\n- Suggest features and discuss them in an issue first.\n- Submit pull requests with tests and documentation.\n- Improve documentation, tutorials and examples.\n- Translate the framework into more languages.
landing.reference.contribute.list.2=- [Contribution guide](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [Issue tracker](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress/issues)\n- [Discussions](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress/discussions)
landing.reference.contribute.text.5=Guidelines
landing.reference.contribute.list.3=- **Coding style:** follow the conventions used across the framework family.\n- **Architecture:** keep responsibilities cleanly scoped to Core, UI, App or Index.\n- **Tests:** bug fixes ship with a regression test; features ship with coverage.\n- **Documentation:** update READMEs, guides or tutorials together with the change.
landing.reference.contribute.list.4=- [Code of conduct](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [Good first issues](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22)
landing.reference.contact.text.1=Reach out
landing.reference.contact.text.2=Contact
landing.reference.contact.text.3=We do not run any external form services or trackers on this site. The fastest way to reach the project is GitHub. For private matters, use the email address below.
landing.reference.contact.text.4=Project communication
landing.reference.contact.text.5=Open an issue for bugs and feature requests, or start a discussion for questions and ideas. This keeps the conversation public and searchable for everyone. For release notes, articles and background on the project, follow the project blog.
landing.reference.contact.list.1=- [Open a new issue](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress/issues/new/choose)\n- [Start a discussion](https://github.com/webexpress-framework/WebExpress/discussions)\n- [GitHub organisation](https://github.com/webexpress-framework)\n- [WebExpress blog](https://webexpress-framework.blogspot.com/)
landing.reference.contact.text.6=The blog is hosted externally on Blogger. Visiting it leaves this site; see the [privacy notice](privacy).
landing.reference.contact.text.7=Direct contact
landing.reference.contact.text.8=Reach the maintainer by email. Your message is sent through your own mail client. This site does not store the message.
landing.reference.contact.text.9=[webexpress-framework@outlook.com](mailto:webexpress-framework@outlook.com)
landing.reference.contact.text.10=By writing to us you only share the data your own mail client transmits. We process it solely to answer your request.
landing.reference.legal.text.1=Privacy first
landing.reference.legal.text.2=Legal & Privacy
landing.reference.legal.text.3=This example reproduces the WebExpress project website using server-rendered controls and scoped fragments. Unlike the static original, the tutorial runs on WebExpress and uses necessary cookies and browser storage.
landing.reference.legal.text.4=Necessary storage, no trackers
landing.reference.legal.text.5=The tutorial uses necessary cookies and browser storage for application features and privacy preferences. This landing page adds no analytics or tracking services.
landing.reference.legal.text.6=No external resources
landing.reference.legal.text.7=All fonts, images and styles are served from this domain. There are no CDN requests and no third-party JavaScript.
landing.reference.legal.text.8=Privacy information
landing.reference.legal.text.9=Read the full [privacy notice](privacy) and the [imprint](https://webexpress-framework.github.io/imprint.html) for details on data handling and responsibility.
